patrone-file-manager (0.2.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Permissions gives other people and groups access by name, as Windows'
    Add... button does: each gets a row with Read, Write and Run (List
    contents, Add and delete, Open for folders) and a button to take it
    away. Made with ACLs (getfacl, setfacl); a folder hands them on to new
    items inside; as administrator through pkexec when needed. The Owner
    and Group rows name who they are, and the mode shows "+" as ls does.
  * Recommends acl, which has getfacl and setfacl.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:05:00 -0500

patrone-file-manager (0.2.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Folder Options closes again after being reopened: a closed dialog
    stayed alive, held by its own close button, and came back with dead
    OK and Cancel buttons. Dialogs now hold themselves weakly.
  * System folder hints show what a folder is for in a plain Purpose
    column in Details (and after the type in Tiles and Content, and in
    tooltips) instead of a tag beside the name.
  * The address bar shows the whole path from This PC, as Windows does;
    what doesn't fit folds into a << button that lists it.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:45:00 -0500

patrone-file-manager (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Tabs keep a fixed width. Dragging a window's only tab moves the window;
    a tab pulled out of the strip (or dragged with Ctrl) joins another
    window's tabs when dropped on its title bar, or opens in a window of its
    own. "Move to new window" moves the tab itself; "Move to window" lists
    the other windows. Files dropped on a tab go into its folder.
  * A tab's close button works again: the tab no longer takes the click.
  * Commands typed in the address bar run in the folder on screen, as in
    Windows: apps with windows directly, anything else in a terminal that
    stays open; Windows' names (cmd, notepad, explorer...) work; cd PLACE
    goes there.
  * System folder hints (View > Show, Folder Options > View): tags saying
    what system folders and well-known files are for, a banner with the
    Windows equivalent, and the matching commands in Permissions.
  * Permissions: changeable owner and group, "Allow running this file as a
    program", the special permissions, applying to everything inside a
    folder, the mode as numbers and letters, and changes as administrator
    through pkexec when they need it.
  * System folders have their own icons; the special folders' emblems and
    the system drive's mark are larger.
  * Text in Patrone's typeface (Noto Sans) at Windows' 9 points, with larger
    icons in the lists; the empty-folder message sits in the middle.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:40:00 -0500

